Changelog:

# SPECIAL THANKS TO BETA TESTERS:
- tasxatzial
- avc1657

# OVERVIEW
- This update introduces minor improvements to the shader's atmosphere, including better fog and new emissives, as well as other features.

# General changes:
- Remade cirrus clouds, now they look twisted and more natural.
- Further reduced artifacts on DoF and Bloom.
- Remade fog, now it looks smoother.
- Near fog now works as ground fog, improving scene depth.
- Reworked how fog colors are calculated.
- Revamped emissives, giving them a better look.
- Sea lanterns, glowstone, torches, and lanterns now glow when handheld. (Requires emissive materials turned on.)
- Selective TAA is now implemented, reducing ghosting in entities. (Inherited from MakeUp)
- Small changes to sun glow.
- Vanilla Sun/moon now cuts off when it is below the horizon.
- Reduced color banding in the sky.
- Small changes to how tonemap treats colors.

# Bugfixes:
- Fixed some black/colorful pixels appearing randomly (mainly on plants and seagrass).
- Fixed some issues with AO in Distant Horizons chunks.
- Fixed a bug that made sign text disappear while using labPBR on 26.3.

